  "phases": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "title": "Drive to the Volga and the bombing",
      "time": "23–26 August 1942",
      "durationSec": 9,
      "narration": "The German 6th Army and 4th Panzer Army attack toward Stalingrad on 23 August 1942, and about 600 Axis aircraft of Luftflotte 4 bomb the largely wooden city over 23–26 August, killing many civilians. Soviet artillery on the east bank and the 62nd and 64th Armies hold the outskirts; by 3 September Axis troops reach the city limits and by 12 September they enter the city proper.",
