      "id": "p7",
      "title": "Winter Storm relief attempt",
      "time": "12–23 December 1942",
      "durationSec": 12,
      "narration": "Manstein's Army Group Don sends the LVII Panzer Corps from Kotelnikovo with Hoth's 4th Panzer Army on 12 December; its 23rd Panzer Division has no more than thirty serviceable tanks at first. By 19 December it is about 48 km from the pocket, but the Soviet 2nd Guards Army (about 90,000 men) has been moved up, Operation Little Saturn threatens Manstein's flank, and the 6th Army, with fuel for only about 30 km, does not break out. Manstein abandons the attempt on 23 December.",
